cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SonicSight
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it, and cite the two
  underlying models listed in the references below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jaafer
    family-names: Mahfoud
  - given-names: Hatem
    family-names: Ibrahim
abstract: >-
  A near-real-time, visually guided audio source separation system
  running on consumer hardware. An Android client captures camera and
  microphone together and streams both to an inference server over
  bidirectional gRPC; the server returns two separated audio tracks and
  a heatmap locating the sound source in the scene. Two pre-trained
  models of different architectures and frameworks are integrated behind
  a single frozen specification registry and share one consumer GPU in
  one process. The study finds that perceptual latency is imposed by the
  models' analysis-window structure rather than by systems engineering.
keywords:
  - audio-visual source separation
  - self-supervised learning
  - gRPC
  - Android
  - algorithmic latency
year: 2026
